<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Texas harvest starts slowly.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Texas harvest starts slowly.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harvesting of hard red winter wheat around Fort Worth, Texas, started slowly over the weekend, and grain dealers said Monday it was still too early to get a clear assessment of the crop quality.</p>
<p>One Kansas dealer said he had heard that protein values ranged from 10 to 15 percent, but he cautioned against drawing too many conclusions based on a few samples.</p>
<p>An Oklahoma dealer said her counterparts in Fort Worth had received about six truckloads of new crop wheat as of Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;They said the crop was looking good and the quality was looking good, but that's only a small sample,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>The dealer said test weights on the sample ranged from 59.7 to 62 lbs.</p>
<p>&quot;Most all of it was rated number one,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, basis bids were mixed Monday, and Gulf bids had tapered off from their recent seasonal highs.  </p>
